concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-1-sec-23-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23 Employer powers etc. of Commissioner"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-23-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner, on behalf of the Commonwealth, has all the rights, duties and powers of an employer in respect of AFP employees.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Commissioner has, in respect of AFP employees, the rights, duties and powers that are prescribed by the regulations." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner, on behalf of the Commonwealth, has all the rights, duties and powers of an employer in respect of AFP employees.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Commissioner has, in respect of AFP employees, the rights, duties and powers that are prescribed by the regulations."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ad0a92205a2771f62bd47acd043d98bac03ae81155b2d0aae17d21ab1fa4436b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "17"^^xsd:integer ;
