concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-1-sec-32-2-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32(3) Retirement on invalidity grounds"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-32-2-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If:  (a) a person is engaged as an AFP employee under section 24 for a period; and  (b) the person completes that period of engagement (the initial period); and  (c) the person is not re-engaged under that section for a further period starting immediately after the end of the initial period; and  (d) the Commissioner certifies in writing that the person’s physical or mental incapacity was the only reason why the person was not so re-engaged; the person is taken, for the purposes of the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 and the Superannuation Act, to have been retired under this section on the day on which the initial period ended.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979  AFP employee is an eligible employee under the Superannuation Act 1976" ;
    skos:definition "(3) If:  (a) a person is engaged as an AFP employee under section 24 for a period; and  (b) the person completes that period of engagement (the initial period); and  (c) the person is not re-engaged under that section for a further period starting immediately after the end of the initial period; and  (d) the Commissioner certifies in writing that the person’s physical or mental incapacity was the only reason why the person was not so re-engaged; the person is taken, for the purposes of the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 and the Superannuation Act, to have been retired under this section on the day on which the initial period ended.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979  AFP employee is an eligible employee under the Superannuation Act 1976"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "57db5a509b8e66c970965c59f1bbb211a6f3e6e206bc7a05a0a5b9b50e016a0f" ;
