ation to such a review; and  (b) give a copy of those reasons to the AFP employee concerned; the regulations may also make provision in relation to:  (c) the exclusion from that copy of any information of a medical or psychiatric nature that the person or body thinks may be prejudicial to the employee’s physical or mental health or well-being; and  (d) the employee nominating a medical practitioner to receive that information.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979" ;
