concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-1-sec-40h a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40H Assignment of duties etc."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-40h ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the duties of an AFP employee, and the place or places at which the duties are to be performed. Determination of terms and conditions while AFP employee outside Australia  (2) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the terms and conditions applying to an AFP employee while the employee is performing duties outside Australia. Duties to meet special operational needs  (3) If:  (a) the Commissioner makes a determination under subsection (1); and  Amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979  Schedule 1  (b) the Commissioner specifies in the determination that the duties concerned are to meet the special operational needs of the Australian Federal Police; the Commissioner may determine in writing the accommodation arrangements that are to apply to the employee, or any allowances the employee is to be paid, while the employee is performing those duties." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the duties of an AFP employee, and the place or places at which the duties are to be performed. Determination of terms and conditions while AFP employee outside Australia  (2) The Commissioner may from time to time determine in writing the terms and conditions applying to an AFP employee while the employee is performing duties outside Australia. Duties to meet special operational needs  (3) If:  (a) the Commissioner makes a determination under subsection (1); and  Amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979  Schedule 1  (b) the Commissioner specifies in the determination that the duties concerned are to meet the special operational needs of the Australian Federal Police; the Commissioner may determine in writing the accommodation arrangements that are to apply to the employee, or any allowances the employee is to be paid, while the employee is performing those duties."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cfca375309a5c5bf5cf6269adcee4a18a090019b04aa2a563bfda4fca0281565" ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-1-sec-40h-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-1-sec-40h-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-1-sec-40h-ss-3 ;
