concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-1-sec-69d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "69D Secondment of persons to assist the Australian Federal Police"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-69d ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner may, by written agreement with a body or organisation, whether within or outside Australia, arrange for a person who:  (a) is employed by that body or organisation; and  (b) has suitable qualifications and experience; to assist the Australian Federal Police in the performance of its functions by performing the functions specified in the agreement.  (2) The terms and conditions (including remuneration and allowances) applicable to a person performing functions under an agreement are those specified in the agreement." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner may, by written agreement with a body or organisation, whether within or outside Australia, arrange for a person who:  (a) is employed by that body or organisation; and  (b) has suitable qualifications and experience; to assist the Australian Federal Police in the performance of its functions by performing the functions specified in the agreement.  (2) The terms and conditions (including remuneration and allowances) applicable to a person performing functions under an agreement are those specified in the agreement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a2f14116617b18b231ad51fcd315df6732459f19c19d0b7f6ef315393866d689" ;
    cof:pageNumber "49"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-1-sec-69d-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-1-sec-69d-ss-2 ;
