    values:originalText "The amendment of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 made by Schedule 2 to this Act applies to acts done at or after the commencing time in relation to:  (a) the Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police, a Deputy Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police, an AFP employee or a special member of the Australian Federal Police (all within the meaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 as in force at and after the commencing time); or  (b) persons seeking to become persons of the kind mentioned in paragraph (a)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-3-sec-25 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "25 Amendments of the Evidence Act 1995"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-25 ;
    values:originalText "Evidence given by police officers (1) Section 33 of the Evidence Act 1995 as in force at and after the commencing time applies as if a reference in that section to a police officer included a reference to a person who was a member or special member of the Australian Federal Police at any time before the commencing time. Exclusion of records of oral questioning (2) Section 86 of the Evidence Act 1995 as in force at and after the commencing time applies as if a reference in that section to an investigating official included a reference to a person who was a member or special member of the Australian Federal Police at any time before the commencing time. Exclusion of evidence of identification by pictures (3) Section 115 of the Evidence Act 1995 as in force at and after the commencing time applies as if a reference in that section to a police officer included a reference to a person who was a member or special member of the Australian Federal Police at any time before the commencing time.  Schedule 3  Application and transitional provisions" ;
    skos:definition "Evidence given by police officers (1) Section 33 of the Evidence Act 1995 as in force at and after the commencing time applies as if a reference in that section to a police officer included a reference to a person who was a member or special member of the Australian Federal Police at any time before the commencing time. Exclusion of records of oral questioning (2) Section 86 of the Evidence Act 1995 as in force at and after the commencing time applies as if a reference in that section to an investigating official included a reference to a person who was a member or special member of the Australian Federal Police at any time before the commencing time. Exclusion of evidence of identification by pictures (3) Section 115 of the Evidence Act 1995 as in force at and after the commencing time applies as if a reference in that section to a police officer included a reference to a person who was a member or special member of the Australian Federal Police at any time before the commencing time.  Schedule 3  Application and transitional provisions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f85ce3014d0dbef9983b4f80bd6e33b75ff7d0113c420894c8c87c35500ff0fd" ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
