concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-3-sec-27 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "27 Amendment of the Migration Act 1958"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-27 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Migration Act 1958 as in force at and after the commencing time applies to a former 147 certificate in the same way as it does to a later 147 certificate. (2) In this item: former 147 certificate means a certificate given under section 147 of the Migration Act 1958 at any time before the commencing time by a member of the Australian Federal Police of a rank not lower than Superintendent.  Application and transitional provisions  Schedule 3 Application and transitional provisions relating to the amendments made by Schedule 2" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Migration Act 1958 as in force at and after the commencing time applies to a former 147 certificate in the same way as it does to a later 147 certificate. (2) In this item: former 147 certificate means a certificate given under section 147 of the Migration Act 1958 at any time before the commencing time by a member of the Australian Federal Police of a rank not lower than Superintendent.  Application and transitional provisions  Schedule 3 Application and transitional provisions relating to the amendments made by Schedule 2"@en ;
