concept:australian-federal-police-legislation-amendment-act-2000-sch-3-sec-29 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29 Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-29 ;
    values:originalText "Continuation of Act in relation to things done before the commencing time (1) The Privacy Act 1988 as in force at and after the commencing time applies to things of the kind mentioned in section 8, 9, 10 or 11 of that Act in relation to members, staff members or special members of the Australian Federal Police that occurred before the commencing time in the same way as it does to such things that occur at or after the commencing time in relation to AFP employees or special members (both within the meaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 as in force at and after the commencing time). Obligations of confidence (2) The amendment of the Privacy Act 1988 made by item 42 of Schedule 2 to this Act applies to obligations of confidence that arise under Part VIII of that Act at or after the commencing time in relation to:  (a) the Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police; or  (b) a Deputy Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police; or  (c) an AFP employee; or  (d) a special member of the Australian Federal Police; (all within the meaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 as in force at and after the commencing time).  Schedule 3  Application and transitional provisions" ;
    skos:definition "Continuation of Act in relation to things done before the commencing time (1) The Privacy Act 1988 as in force at and after the commencing time applies to things of the kind mentioned in section 8, 9, 10 or 11 of that Act in relation to members, staff members or special members of the Australian Federal Police that occurred before the commencing time in the same way as it does to such things that occur at or after the commencing time in relation to AFP employees or special members (both within the meaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 as in force at and after the commencing time). Obligations of confidence (2) The amendment of the Privacy Act 1988 made by item 42 of Schedule 2 to this Act applies to obligations of confidence that arise under Part VIII of that Act at or after the commencing time in relation to:  (a) the Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police; or  (b) a Deputy Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police; or  (c) an AFP employee; or  (d) a special member of the Australian Federal Police; (all within the meaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 as in force at and after the commencing time).  Schedule 3  Application and transitional provisions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "29cc3f346ba68bed2e71be197f6c4956a746e18d63381ff903726ea734b13919" ;
    cof:pageNumber "79"^^xsd:integer ;
